      why: "Politeness in English lives in the verb and the hedge — “could I”, “would you mind”, “just” — not in the pronoun. The same “you” covers a stranger and a lifelong friend.",
      ifYouSwitch: "Dropping the hedge changes everything: “Give me a coffee” is grammatical and rude, whereas “Could I have a coffee?” is grammatical and warm. Spanish speakers often sound blunter in English than they intend, because they expect the pronoun to carry the politeness."
